{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvakcCwkSSxmRAzs112L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't decide yet. Spend a week or two on a cheap analysis, then decide against a break-even number.**\n\nThe evidence so far is thin but not trivial. Three requests and one lost deal in a month is an anecdote. But HR data is sensitive, and you're moving up-market, so the pattern may well grow. The analysis costs almost nothing next to £60k and six months.\n\n**Before deciding:**\n1. **Code the 140 lost deals.** Don't rely on the loss-reason field. Reps often pick \"price\" or \"no decision\" when security was the real blocker, so read the notes and emails for security, questionnaire or SOC 2 mentions.\n2. **Check the open and stalled pipeline.** Count how many deals are blocked on or have asked about security, and their value.\n3. **Ask the three prospects, and any lost deal that cited it, what would satisfy them.** A Type I report, ISO 27001, a pen-test summary or a completed questionnaire might do. Type I is faster and cheaper, and is a common first step.\n4. **Set the break-even.** £60k divided by your average first-year contract value gives the deals SOC 2 must win or save. If the average is £20k, that's about three deals, plus the internal time cost, which I'd assume is substantial.\n\n**Decision rule (set the thresholds beforehand):**\n- **Start** if security blocked a meaningful share of enterprise losses or pipeline, with value comfortably above break-even.\n- **Drop** if the data shows almost nothing beyond the one deal.\n- **Middle path:** if the picture is ambiguous, build the cheaper interim assets (a trust page, a pen test, a standard questionnaire answer pack) and re-check in a quarter.\n\nRemember that SOC 2 won't help deals in the next six months, so interim assets matter either way."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3445,"cache_read_input_tokens":5036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3445},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a2ac656-4b13-489b-a822-55a28f2ab857","uuid":"f5924a9f-06e9-4f32-abb5-7e3603c3a652","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:09:40.798Z","request_id":"req_011Cfvakbrrtyt7Xa9HGMnWd"}
